WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.380
[TRACE — Telemetry & Tuning Platform]

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.880
A rider says it hit too hard on the exit.
Then what?

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:15.880
[THE DAY HAS ONE QUESTION]
One objective, one team
Every role opens to the same test objective — not twelve competing dashboards.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:23.880
[RIDER MARKS THE MOMENT]
Anchored to the track, not memory
The report is pinned to a corner and a lap, so it can be found in the data.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:33.880
[THE TRACE IS READ, NOT ASSUMED]
Every lap at that corner
Throttle, slip and RPM are correlated across the whole session — not one lucky lap.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:44.880
[RANKED CAUSES, COMPUTED CONFIDENCE]
It shows its work
Confidence comes from the data — capped when a channel is degraded, never certain.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.880
The engineer recommends. It never decides.
Only a person with the right role can approve a change.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:57.880
[A BOUNDED CHANGE]
Inside the validated envelope
Revision B moves the partial-throttle region within tuner-set limits — 26 cells, nothing else.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.880
[NO PATH TO THE ECU]
The bike stays protected
TRACE never writes to an ECU. It issues a change sheet a person performs in the manufacturer's own software.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:16.880
[WHAT CHANGED · WHAT HAPPENED · WHAT CAUSED IT]
The rider preferred it. The data disagreed.
Rider confidence rose 3 points while the best lap went 1.79s slower — and the uncontrolled variable is flagged.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:23.880
[THE DECISION IS RECORDED]
A feeling never becomes the baseline
Every revision keeps its status, its evidence and its lineage — so next season knows why.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:29.380
Most tools would have shipped that change.
The rider liked it. TRACE showed the lap times anyway.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:35.880
[TRACE] Evidence, not opinion — on every change. trace-4qya.onrender.com. Phase 1 runs on simulated telemetry, labeled on every screen. No ECU write path exists in this build.
